tools/feedback: the feedback form
=================================

mkfeedback.py builds docs/feedback/decisions-feedback.txt, a plain-text form (at most 100
columns, no Markdown) for reading and answering in a pager with an editor.  Its entries come
from the open items of Appendix J, the proposals of Appendix H, the confirmation list
(tools/feedback/confirmations.txt), the status ledger (docs/decisions-and-status.md:
subjects in the air, and to-do subjects whose details are pending) and two standing decisions (W.1 the first FPGA board, W.3 the merge of the pcc branch); the codes V.M, V.H, V.I, V.P and V.N of the confirmation list are in the file named above, and a question that has a place elsewhere in the form is asked only there.
Each entry has a stable ID (J.n.k, H.<statement>, V.<code>, S.<subject>, W.n), an order number,
a line AFFECTS OPCODES: yes|maybe|no (the items that may change opcodes, mnemonics or the
encoding come first), the issue, lettered options, and the answer lines DECISION: and NOTE:.

The entries are generated from the manual fragments, so the generator must be re-run after
chapter edits (the form is a tracked file; "mkfeedback.py --check" tells whether it is stale).
The ID of an entry does not change between runs; the text of the options does when the
fragment changes, so answers should be ingested before the form is regenerated.

Use:
  python3 tools/feedback/mkfeedback.py            write docs/feedback/decisions-feedback.txt
  winless open docs/feedback/decisions-feedback.txt
        edit: on each DECISION: line type a letter, several letters, "other: text" or "defer";
        put reasons on NOTE: (continuation lines indented); make annotations as usual; write.
  python3 tools/feedback/ingest.py                print the Markdown report, write answers.json
  python3 tools/feedback/ingest.py --status       counts: answered, deferred, open, by opcode effect
  tools/feedback/test-feedback.sh                 generate, simulate an edit, ingest, check

ingest.py reads the annotations of the form from the pager's SQLite database
(~/.local/share/winless/winless.db, or --db) and attaches each to the entry whose line range
contains it.  It writes only answers.json (beside the form, or --json), never another file.

Manual pages: mkfeedback.1, ingest.1.  License: see COPYING at the root of the repository.
